# NERC Analogy Map

This file maps NERC RC exam concepts to analogies drawn from YOUR professional background.
The tutor and comprehension skills read this file before every response.

## How to Use This Template

1. Copy this file to `reference/analogy-map.md`
2. For each domain, pick the analogy source that fits YOUR experience
3. Replace the example analogies with ones from your own work
4. The more specific and personal the analogy, the better it sticks

The example column below uses generic IT/infrastructure analogies as placeholders.

## TRANSMISSION -> (YOUR BACKGROUND)
| NERC Concept | Your Analogy |
|---|---|
| Power lines | Network cables / bandwidth links |
| Transformers | Routers / switches (protocol translation) |
| Thermal ratings | Throughput limits / bandwidth caps |
| Power flow | Traffic routing / data flow |
| ATC | Available bandwidth for new traffic |
| Voltage | Signal quality / integrity |

